

Strategy design pattern is generally used to avoid open closed principle violation and injection of different strategy at runtime.

// It is famously used in sort() method

List<String> list = List.of("Mahendra", "Ram", "Krishna");

list.stream()
    .sorted((a, b) -> a.length() - b.length())  // here the comparator is the different strategy which can be passed
    .toList();

also in Collections.sort(list, ageComparator);
